From: vincenzopio <43883474+vincenzopio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 23:26:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] xgameruntime: Keep the multithreaded apartment alive from
 initialization.

The runtime's own threads (task queue workers, the Xodus socket thread) activate WinRT classes
such as Windows.Storage.Streams.Buffer without initializing COM. With no thread of the process in
the multithreaded apartment, RoGetActivationFactory() fails there with CO_E_NOTINITIALIZED. Call
CoIncrementMTAUsage() once from InitializeApiImplEx2(), as Windows components do, so that those
threads use the MTA implicitly.

Original work for macrock (LGPL-2.1-or-later).

Topic: winrt-mta
---
 src/main.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index 20b8d3cc0e9f66edec201b2695761d8a40ba1af1..84f40f462ecaaf03893556189e9d0d6e918c482a 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -55,12 +55,18 @@ BOOL WINAPI DllMain( HINSTANCE hinst, DWORD reason, void *reserved )
     return TRUE;
 }
 
+static CO_MTA_USAGE_COOKIE mtaCookie;
+
 HRESULT WINAPI InitializeApiImplEx2( ULONG gdkVer, ULONG gsVer, char mode, const INITIALIZE_OPTIONS *options )
 {
     HRESULT status = S_OK;
 
     TRACE( "gdkVer %ld, gsVer %ld, mode %d, options %p.\n", gdkVer, gsVer, mode, options );
 
+    /* The runtime's threads use WinRT without initializing COM: keep the MTA alive for them. */
+    if ( !mtaCookie && FAILED( status = CoIncrementMTAUsage( &mtaCookie ) ) )
+        ERR( "CoIncrementMTAUsage failed, hr %#lx.\n", status );
+
     if ( !socketInitialized )
     {
         if ( SUCCEEDED( status = xodus_ipclayer->InitializeSocket() ) )
